## Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully implemented Vercel Web Analytics for the Next.js project.

### Changes Made

**Modified Files:**
1. `app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics component integration
   - Imported `Analytics` from `@vercel/analytics/next`
   - Added `<Analytics />` component inside the body element

2. `package.json` - Added dependency
   - Added `@vercel/analytics: ^2.0.1` to dependencies

3. `package-lock.json` - Updated lockfile
   - Installed 372 new packages as dependencies of @vercel/analytics
   - Lockfile updated to ensure consistent dependency resolution

### Implementation Details

- **Framework Detected:** Next.js 16.2.7 with App Router
- **Package Manager:** npm (confirmed by package-lock.json)
- **Installation Method:** Fetched latest instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- **Integration Pattern:** Followed official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router

The Analytics component was added to the root layout following Next.js App Router best practices:
- Imported from `@vercel/analytics/next` for seamless Next.js integration
- Placed at the end of the body tag to ensure it doesn't interfere with page rendering
- Provides automatic route tracking for all pages in the application

### Verification Steps Completed

✓ Package installed successfully using npm
✓ TypeScript type checking passed (npx tsc --noEmit)
✓ Code is syntactically correct (no errors in our changes during lint)
✓ Changes staged with git

### Next Steps for Deployment

To enable analytics data collection in production:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Navigate to the project's Analytics tab in Vercel Dashboard
3. Click "Enable" to activate Web Analytics
4. Analytics data will appear after deployment and user visits

### Notes

- The build test encountered a pre-existing Supabase configuration error (missing supabaseUrl), which is unrelated to the Analytics implementation
- Pre-existing linting errors exist in other files (login/page.tsx, page.tsx) but are not related to this change
- The Analytics component is lightweight and will not impact page load performance
- Data collection is fully GDPR compliant and privacy-friendly (no cookies required)
